  "description": "BUCMIW crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C8 H20 N1 O2 1+,C100 H200 Gd8 Mn5 N8 O64 1-,5(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.419-4.196 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.28-119.02°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C118H235Gd8Mn5N14O66. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 12 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
